/**
 * Serializes the {@code message} into an {@link OutputStream} with a length prefix.
 *
 * @param out The {@link OutputStream} to write to
 * @param message The message to serialize
 * @param schema The {@link Schema} for the message
 * @param buffer A {@link LinkedBuffer} to use for temporary storage
 * @param <T> The type of the message
 * @return The number of bytes written to the stream
 * @throws IOException if an I/O error occurs
 */
public static <T> int writeDelimitedTo(OutputStream out, T message, Schema<T> schema, LinkedBuffer buffer) throws IOException {
    // Calculate the encoded size of the message
    int size = schema.getMessageSize(message);

    // Write the size of the message as a varint
    out.write(size);

    // Write the message to the stream
    CodedOutputStream codedOutput = CodedOutputStream.newInstance(out, buffer);
    schema.writeTo(codedOutput, message);
    codedOutput.flush();

    // Return the number of bytes written to the stream
    return size + 1;
}
```
Note that this method is generic, so it can be used to serialize any message type that has a corresponding schema. The schema must implement the {@code Schema<T>} interface, which provides the necessary methods for serializing and deserializing messages of type {@code T}.

